# Build context exclusions.
#
# The application tree is delivered as deploy/app.tar (see deploy/build-image.sh),
# not as directory COPYs, so the symlink exclusions this file used to carry are
# no longer needed -- tar preserves symlinks natively, cycles included.
#
# What remains is the rule that matters: secrets must never enter the build
# context, so they cannot be baked into an image by a careless COPY.

deploy/.env
deploy/nginx/certs/
PaintomicsServer/src/conf/serverconf.py
.git/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.DS_Store
*.log

# The reference GTF library. It is bind-mounted into the container at run time
# (see the ./gtf mount in deploy/compose.yaml), so it must never enter the
# image -- and, more urgently, never enter the build context: at 6.6 GB it took
# the context from ~800 MB to 7.4 GB, and every build after that produced an
# image whose rootfs was missing /bin/sh while still reporting success.
deploy/gtf/
